{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0248","billNumberShort":"H.B. 248","billNumberLong":"HB0248S01","fileNumber":"2026FL0487","shortTitle":"Family Law Modifications","currentSubVersion":"1","currentMinVersion":"3","primeSponsor":"WARDR","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Ward, Raymond P.","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MCKELMK","floorSponsorName":"Sen. McKell, Michael K.","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill addresses family law issues related to spousal support, child support, custody, and parent-time.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the duties of the Office of Recovery Services with regard to spousal support;<hr><ltbullet>requires the director of the Office of Recovery Services to hold certain meetings for obligees and obligors and places a sunset date on the requirement;<hr><ltbullet>creates a reporting requirement for the director of the Office of Recovery Services and places a sunset date on the reporting requirement;<hr><ltbullet>addresses the collection of spousal support by the Office of Recovery Services after a child support obligation ends;<hr><ltbullet>allows a certain amount of money from a monthly child support payment to pass through to a family who is receiving public assistance on and after July 1, 2028;<hr><ltbullet>addresses the suspension of a driver license by the Office of Recovery Services, including the suspension of an individual's driver license when the individual is in arrears of at least $35,000;<hr><ltbullet>modifies the information provided by the Online Court Assistance Program;<hr><ltbullet>provides that a delinquent payment for child support accrues interest on and after July 1, 2027; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes. ","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Jacqueline Carlton","fiscalAnalyst":"Josh Pittman","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/17/2026","trackingID":"QQKPMSPKTX","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-13 15:49:12.967","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbered Bill Publicly Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-13 15:49:12.967","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LLFA","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill assigned to staff for fiscal analysis for HB0248","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Analyst","actionDate":"2026-01-13 15:49:18.100","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ bill sent to agencies for fiscal input for HB0248","owner":"Legislative Fiscal Agency","actionDate":"2026-01-13 15:49:18.100","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA2","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"House/ received bill from Legislative Research","owner":"Clerk of the House","actionDate":"2026-01-14 14:15:00.000","actionClass":"H","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"HRECLRGC","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"House/ 1st reading (Introduced)","owner":"House Rules Committee","actionDate":"2026-01-20 15:38:26.000","actionClass":"H","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"HREAD1","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note sent to sponsor for HB0248","owner":"Version Sponsor","actionDate":"2026-01-22 19:22:17.590","actionClass":"F","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LFA3","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"LFA/ fiscal note publicly available for HB0248","owner":"Released","actionDate":"2026-01-22 20:55:13.722","actionClass":"F","